o pass by me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.561,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"100029ff5cb265604ef967798407c0cc2159a0ec1cf7540ab921354c23633ca7","compact":"70541e57931ffd6ce6a963c3ec75cf4637f13d9a5a2acfbc27f7455949765ba8","nasal":"70541e57931ffd6ce6a963c3ec75cf4637f13d9a5a2acfbc27f7455949765ba8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-46-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":46,"verse":18,"english":"O timid damsel, truly shall you repent afterwards if you did disregard me, like to Urvasi kicking Pururavā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.702,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"315fd640197da1972294f3e5d54006cd95ad12138f62643b02fd17f41bc8adf5","compact":"406e7db417c388f9e6a461bfda3cec0f1084937f204f90664d60d468426076d7","nasal":"406e7db417c388f9e6a461bfda3cec0f1084937f204f90664d60d468426076d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-46-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":46,"verse":19,"english":"Rāma is a human being and is not even equal to a finger of mine in battle. By your good luck have I come to you-do you give yourself up to me, O you of a beautiful countenance. Being thus addressed by him, Vaidehi exceedingly wroth and with blood-red eyes spoke to that Lord of Rākşasas in the lonely forest, these bold words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e00128eafc7b580ff602c6142ed3cd5dd83fb112e9f8e32c8b2e2ebf6ad5405","compact":"4d1d10b1d2a1055e6cf2a56cd535198f5bdd1038ca3521905692a9bb9d994eca","nasal":"4d1d10b1d2a1055e6cf2a56cd535198f5bdd1038ca3521905692a9bb9d994eca"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-46-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":46,"verse":20,"english":"How do you wish to perpetrate such an impious deed after introducing as your brother that highly worshipful Kubera adored by all the deities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1d291f0456d2c63c03d8204f17761673a107f55e116d7491e37e1a16f7cfe98e","compact":"a0d59e6429a56c528ff612e3593748f8f9271b6d69663f1a19470f77fbcf556e","nasal":"0081b072a989d0e0aa08f9bce581e9ae8e1cff7a2cb6aa7cc34018f543a71d70"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-46-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":46,"verse":21,"english":"O Rāvana, surely shall all the Räkşasas meet with death, who have such a stupid, harsh and lustful person like you for their king.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6be924c11f592d4a893706ddc90531bb8079a127e0182cd168fab223ae70bd7a","compact":"d4d1769f548176629cb84b0ef74f62b5010fc195dccb84c98989fef372b3ff21","nasal":"d084b77a5d2016ec110a7b0ec6385ceafb3a4a5031889b1b2911969de3e18e0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-46-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":46,"verse":22,"english":"One can breathe on this earth carrying away Indra's wife, Śacī—but stealing me, the wife of Rāma, no body shall be able to live in peace.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.515,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-48-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3046022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1983f9d19417670